1
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:03,860
Eli...

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:07,570
Do you know much I love you?

3
00:00:07,570 --> 00:00:10,410
How much I always want to protect you...

4
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:14,190
Do you want to go mad as much as I do?

5
00:00:14,190 --> 00:00:15,500
I want you to know everything.

6
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:22,130
Lady Elianna!

7
00:00:24,130 --> 00:00:27,510
I know you're in there!
Come out like a proper lady!

8
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:29,760
I'm telling you that now is *not* a good time!

9
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,510
Can I at least run away?

10
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:33,270
Lady Elianna!

11
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:36,520
Every single time, the pests come
just when we get to the good part.

12
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,730
Is this some sort of tanuki curse at work?

13
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:47,040
The Holy Night's Banquet Where the Butterflies Dance

14
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:47,040
The Holy Night's Banquet Where the Butterflies Dance

15
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:47,040
The Holy Night's Banquet Where the Butterflies Dance

16
00:00:43,230 --> 00:00:44,020
Um...

17
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:50,410
I would like to have a talk with Elianna,
just the two of us.

18
00:00:50,410 --> 00:00:53,660
Lady Sharon, there's no need to be shy.

19
00:00:55,620 --> 00:01:00,130
Lady Sharon, what do you need
to talk to me about?

20
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:06,670
At the Holy Night's Banquet, please let me
be Prince Christopher's partner in your place.

21
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:13,340
You will be compensated, of course.

22
00:01:14,550 --> 00:01:18,520
If you would be willing to trade with me,
I'll let you borrow this as thanks.

23
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:21,640
Could that... possibly be...

24
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:25,960
Yes, the ship's log of Captain Vigo,
also known as the King of the Seas,

25
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:27,730
written by the man himself.

26
00:01:27,730 --> 00:01:29,720
Captain Vigo...

27
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:33,910
Historically, he was first to accomplish
the conquest of the eastern ship routes.

28
00:01:35,370 --> 00:01:37,740
Because he died young and on foreign land

29
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:44,000
his name and achievements are given precedence
over the reality of his voyage,

30
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,540
and he's become a legendary figure.

31
00:01:46,540 --> 00:01:49,300
What tales of adventure did he record?

32
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:53,890
How could you propose such a thing, Lady Sharon?!

33
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:58,150
My grandfather said I could use it however I wanted!

34
00:01:58,150 --> 00:01:59,430
There are limits to these sorts—

35
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:01,140
Lady Elianna.

36
00:02:01,140 --> 00:02:02,570
What do you say?

37
00:02:02,570 --> 00:02:08,860
I obviously cannot give this to you,
but I can lend it to you while I'm staying here.

38
00:02:18,290 --> 00:02:19,740
<i>I know...</i>

39
00:02:20,900 --> 00:02:23,750
<i>I cannot have it both ways.</i>

40
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,500
<i>Right... Of course.</i>

41
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:29,580
I can't do that.

42
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:30,250
Wah?

43
00:02:30,860 --> 00:02:36,590
Your silence in deciding was extraordinarily long,
and you look like you're about to break out in tears...

44
00:02:36,590 --> 00:02:38,640
<i>You're imagining things, Your Highness.</i>

45
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:44,190
I have a fair idea of why you are so insistent
about myself being your partner, Lady Sharon.

46
00:02:44,190 --> 00:02:46,150
However, is this something you decided on,

47
00:02:46,150 --> 00:02:49,150
or is this the will of the Miseral Dukedom?

48
00:02:49,150 --> 00:02:51,530
W-Well, I...

49
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:53,530
Lady Sharon decided this on her own.

50
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:54,400
Elen!

51
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:57,160
Please consider your position.

52
00:02:57,160 --> 00:03:02,600
Lady Mireille even told you
to watch your speech and actions, did she not?

53
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,740
But...

54
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:05,460
But, this is wrong!

55
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:09,290
My sister Mireille is the celebrated
"Pearl Princess of Miseral"!

56
00:03:09,610 --> 00:03:10,420
And yet...

57
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:13,920
She was married to a Count Lamond,
who's 25 years older than her,

58
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:16,380
then he passes away in the blink of an eye...

59
00:03:16,380 --> 00:03:18,680
and she can't expect to get a marriage proposal.

60
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:24,560
Lady Mireille deserves happiness
more than anyone else in the whole country!

61
00:03:25,890 --> 00:03:28,060
You mustn't take your anger out on books!

62
00:03:30,050 --> 00:03:31,520
Come on!

63
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:34,940
It’s your fault for being here, Bibliophile Princess!

64
00:03:36,590 --> 00:03:39,780
That's where Mireille belongs!

65
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:42,450
You care for nothing but books, right?

66
00:03:42,450 --> 00:03:44,830
Then go hole yourself up in the library!

67
00:03:45,080 --> 00:03:45,810
Lady Sharon.

68
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:47,210
I can't do that.

69
00:03:48,880 --> 00:03:53,840
It's certainly true that I am a bookworm
who has no interest in anything but books, but...

70
00:03:53,840 --> 00:03:58,840
the feelings that I have for Prince Christopher
are as real as anyone else's.

71
00:03:59,390 --> 00:04:03,100
I could never give up my place
next to His Highness.

72
00:04:04,890 --> 00:04:06,270
Lady Sharon.

73
00:04:06,270 --> 00:04:08,350
Are you trying to spoil the friendship

74
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:12,670
between Miseral and Sauslind
with your own self-centered desires?

75
00:04:13,590 --> 00:04:14,710
But...

76
00:04:14,710 --> 00:04:17,560
We are beyond the point
where you can resolve things by crying.

77
00:04:17,560 --> 00:04:19,490
You owe Lady Elianna an apology.

78
00:04:23,850 --> 00:04:29,250
Lady Sharon, it seems you have Elianna all wrong.

79
00:04:31,390 --> 00:04:32,630
Eli...

80
00:04:32,630 --> 00:04:35,420
When you had just become my fiancée,

81
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:39,550
you sent away for books related to
medicinal herbs from each country, right?

82
00:04:39,550 --> 00:04:40,970
Why did you do that?

83
00:04:41,620 --> 00:04:45,330
I was curious about the pharmaceutical knowledge
of other countries.

84
00:04:45,330 --> 00:04:46,520
Also...

85
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:52,360
I’d learned that research into treatments
for the Ashen Nightmare had come to a standstill.

86
00:04:52,360 --> 00:04:56,900
I thought other books from other countries
might provide us an alternate perspective.

87
00:04:57,250 --> 00:05:00,450
But that illness is already gone, isn't it?

88
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:03,820
It has only temporarily been resolved.

89
00:05:04,340 --> 00:05:06,830
It may all happen again someday.

90
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:11,180
So you focusing on the Azul Region this whole time

91
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:13,210
was also due to research on the Ashen Nightmare?

92
00:05:14,010 --> 00:05:16,130
That as well,

93
00:05:16,130 --> 00:05:18,510
but in the fairy tales of the Azul Region,

94
00:05:18,510 --> 00:05:21,840
there are a lot of stories about children without parents.

95
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:24,800
When I looked into it,

96
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,390
I learned that there were many villages

97
00:05:26,390 --> 00:05:30,410
where the parents made a living
away from home like in the Corba Village.

98
00:05:30,410 --> 00:05:35,230
I thought it was sad
that the families couldn't live together.

99
00:05:35,540 --> 00:05:36,590
For that reason,

100
00:05:36,590 --> 00:05:41,890
I thought it would be nice if there were something
to base their lifestyles on in the impoverished lands.

101
00:05:41,890 --> 00:05:45,170
But isn’t that kind of...beyond your ability to fix?

102
00:05:45,170 --> 00:05:48,120
We can't make every territory in the country prosperous.

103
00:05:48,360 --> 00:05:53,500
As the nobility, "we can't do anything about that"
are words that must never leave our mouths.

104
00:05:55,050 --> 00:05:57,570
The reason we are not exposed to the elements,

105
00:05:57,570 --> 00:06:02,630
dress in beautiful clothing, and eat elaborate foods

106
00:06:02,990 --> 00:06:05,760
is because that is all supported by the people.

107
00:06:07,390 --> 00:06:08,760
Excuse me.

108
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:13,390
May I ask the reason the shells
from the Corba Village caught your eye?

109
00:06:13,390 --> 00:06:18,910
Originally, it started when I heard from my brother

110
00:06:18,910 --> 00:06:23,240
that the pigments used in the wall paintings
in prehistoric times were made from shells.

111
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:26,120
Then, you decided on Corba Village's Milulu clam?

112
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:31,660
Yes, but... as of right now,
I haven't found any use for it besides in paintings.

113
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:34,670
Did you talk about that in front of my mother too?

114
00:06:34,990 --> 00:06:37,040
Huh? Yes.

115
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:40,300
Lady Sharon, do you understand?

116
00:06:41,220 --> 00:06:46,180
Elianna, during these four years,
has advanced research on the remedy,

117
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:50,510
and searched for ways to enrich impoverished lands.

118
00:06:50,510 --> 00:06:53,560
Even if she did not have the title
of fiancée of the crown prince,

119
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:56,810
I feel she would have done something.

120
00:06:57,120 --> 00:07:01,070
That is precisely why
the people of Sauslind stand behind Elianna.

121
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,690
But...

122
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:06,740
Then why was it so widespread that the Yule Lovers

123
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:09,200
are Your Highness and Mireille's love story?

124
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:13,140
It's because you two have loved
each other since childhood, right?

125
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,550
That handwriting...

126
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:26,840
it's Mireille's!

127
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:31,100
I knew you two were still having intimate exchanges!

128
00:07:31,590 --> 00:07:36,350
The "Yule Lovers"<i> is</i> a story
about Your Highness and Mireille!

129
00:07:36,350 --> 00:07:38,730
Eli! That isn't the case at all.

130
00:07:38,730 --> 00:07:39,820
Sit down.

131
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:48,450
He's like a husband resigned to confess to his affair.

132
00:07:48,450 --> 00:07:50,370
And there's even hard evidence.

133
00:07:50,630 --> 00:07:54,140
Glen, you seem like you want
permanent residence in Miseral.

134
00:07:54,140 --> 00:07:56,750
I'll get you just the paperwork you need later.

135
00:07:57,090 --> 00:07:59,130
Why only me?!

136
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:04,800
About that love story...

137
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:07,130
I've suspect there's a motive behind it.

138
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:08,630
A motive?

139
00:08:08,970 --> 00:08:12,000
I hear that dukes who treated Lady Mireille so coldly

140
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:16,550
also caused damage to the national interest
in an accident at sea several years earlier.

141
00:08:16,550 --> 00:08:19,270
They seem desperate to regain their honor.

142
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:20,650
And?

143
00:08:20,650 --> 00:08:24,570
They set their sights on the popularity of Lady Mireille,
known as the "Pearl Princess,"

144
00:08:24,570 --> 00:08:26,530
who is also supported by the citizens,

145
00:08:26,530 --> 00:08:29,410
and it isn't odd that they would consider using her.

146
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:32,280
Use... Mireille?

147
00:08:33,780 --> 00:08:35,160
I see.

148
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:40,290
If Lady Lamond weren't a widow,
this love story wouldn't be possible.

149
00:08:40,290 --> 00:08:45,340
No way, Duke Lamond died...
and not due to an accident?!

150
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:51,400
Now, I also haven't looked that far into it,
and this is just speculation at the most.

151
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,350
That can't be...

152
00:08:53,350 --> 00:08:54,510
I get it!

153
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:58,430
My sister Mireille requested help
from Your Highness in this letter, right?

154
00:09:00,190 --> 00:09:03,940
Unfortunately, it isn't something as endearing as that.

155
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:09,200
It seems Lady Mireille has been doing
her own investigating into this matter

156
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:12,950
and noticed my own investigations.

157
00:09:13,450 --> 00:09:16,290
We made deals and mutual disclosures and she decided

158
00:09:16,290 --> 00:09:21,830
"We will settle Miseral's internal problems on our own,
and there is no need for any help at all."

159
00:09:22,350 --> 00:09:25,460
Quite bold of her, actually.

160
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:32,800
At the same time, she says, "The one who is like
a dear sister to me may cause a bit of trouble,

161
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:36,850
but I expect you will be tolerant
of the fanciful tales of a child."

162
00:09:36,850 --> 00:09:38,350
She concludes by saying

163
00:09:38,350 --> 00:09:47,320
she sincerely congratulates me for the marriage
with the daughter of the Marquis Bernstein, my first love.

164
00:09:48,190 --> 00:09:49,650
I deeply apologize.

165
00:09:49,650 --> 00:09:53,000
I will offer my apologies on Lady Sharon's behalf.

166
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:58,490
I'm afraid I must make an excuse,
but Lady Sharon's mother is sickly,

167
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:03,210
and Lady Mireille is the one who has taken care
of her since she was a child.

168
00:10:03,610 --> 00:10:11,670
Consequently, that has led to excessive behaviour,
but we ask for your kindness and generosity.

169
00:10:11,670 --> 00:10:14,090
This is just like "The Piglet's Beloved Dimples".

170
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:17,100
Oh, I know that tale.

171
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:20,850
There was an orphaned piglet named Rue.

172
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:23,020
Rue was scrawny and looked unappetizing,

173
00:10:23,020 --> 00:10:25,230
and the people around him
didn't think he'd fetch a good price,

174
00:10:25,230 --> 00:10:32,240
but a young girl who was orphaned just like Rue
raised him and showed him kindness.

175
00:10:32,820 --> 00:10:36,240
The girl fell in love with the son of a Lord.

176
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:40,700
Rue knew of the girl's desire
to catch the boy's eye no matter what it took,

177
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:43,000
so he thought hard about it.

178
00:10:43,310 --> 00:10:44,370
He knew what to do!

179
00:10:44,370 --> 00:10:50,000
He would become the village's
most delicious-looking pig and catch the eye of the lord!

180
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:55,080
It was all because he wanted to see the happy face
of the girl who had dimples when she smiled...

181
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:59,600
So, what happened to the piglet?

182
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:02,430
It's a pig, so it got eaten in the end, right?

183
00:11:02,430 --> 00:11:04,600
You're really heartless, aren't you?

184
00:11:06,190 --> 00:11:12,480
From that letter, I know that Lady Mireille
even now still yearns deeply for Earl Lamond.

185
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:17,490
The actions you take on account of others
will not necessarily produce only good results.

186
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:20,720
They wore on me as well this time.

187
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:26,500
For the piglet's... ah, pardon me, for Lady Sharon's sake,
let's forget this ever happened.

188
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:28,830
We thank you, Your Highness.

189
00:11:28,830 --> 00:11:31,670
Now, Lady Sharon, let's go.

190
00:11:34,890 --> 00:11:38,010
Who is he calling a "piglet"?!

191
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:42,490
She is very much like a piglet.

192
00:12:24,060 --> 00:12:26,490
Ah, Elianna.

193
00:12:26,490 --> 00:12:28,690
It's as if the room has instantly become more dazzling.

194
00:12:29,530 --> 00:12:32,440
Thank you, Your Majesty.

195
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,270
Yes, like—

196
00:12:34,270 --> 00:12:37,440
You're like a single rose, just begun to bloom.

197
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,600
Oh, my.

198
00:12:39,780 --> 00:12:42,450
The red shading may be a bit too strong...

199
00:12:43,030 --> 00:12:45,200
There's still room for improvement.

200
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:50,620
My mother dyed that dress
using the dye of the Milulu clam.

201
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:51,330
Oh?

202
00:12:51,330 --> 00:12:56,210
I had it tailored by my personal designer
based on what you said.

203
00:12:57,720 --> 00:13:01,550
Whether or not the Corba Village and
the Azul Region can become prosperous

204
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:04,300
depends on your publicity.

205
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:06,790
Give it your full effort.

206
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:08,850
Queen Henrietta...

207
00:13:09,190 --> 00:13:14,730
It's all right if I occasionally make use of your ideas
instead of Chris doing it all the time.

208
00:13:15,090 --> 00:13:21,740
Do you hate that Lady Dauner tried to make
a fashionable dress with Eli's idea so much?

209
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:23,990
Of course I do.

210
00:13:23,990 --> 00:13:26,370
And you're responsible too!

211
00:13:26,830 --> 00:13:32,500
Do you know of anyone who would just stand idly by
as their own ideas were poached?

212
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:34,000
N-No...

213
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,340
And making such a tacky dress...

214
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:42,510
Since it originally was your idea,
I had no choice but to agree it was nice...

215
00:13:43,130 --> 00:13:48,890
But make sure you use the power you display
when protecting others for yourself as well.

216
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:54,510
I don't believe that people who can't value themselves
are able to protect others.

217
00:13:56,070 --> 00:13:57,400
Yes...

218
00:13:57,400 --> 00:14:00,150
Thank you very much, Mother.

219
00:14:01,950 --> 00:14:04,170
I was reprimanding you for your behavior.

220
00:14:04,170 --> 00:14:06,320
Who would thank someone for that?

221
00:14:06,320 --> 00:14:07,410
Yes.

222
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:11,400
Now, about Sara...

223
00:14:12,270 --> 00:14:13,040
Yes?

224
00:14:13,590 --> 00:14:17,540
I am also to blame for disobedience
by a maid of the inner palace.

225
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:22,050
It seems like the one who leaked your words
was from a frequent company visitor,

226
00:14:22,050 --> 00:14:24,550
and was in communication with the Dorud Company.

227
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:31,060
The inefficiencies in the vetting process of those
who frequently visit is also under my area of authority.

228
00:14:31,060 --> 00:14:33,570
I must offer you an apology.

229
00:14:34,260 --> 00:14:35,190
There's no need...

230
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:39,320
Sara was removed from the maids,
and I have demoted her.

231
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:43,900
She'll be starting from scratch in her new position,

232
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:48,760
but when she returns,
she must become your devoted maid.

233
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:51,950
Yes, Mother.

234
00:14:56,740 --> 00:15:01,280
Had you only dealt with
your own political opponents from the start,

235
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:03,470
this would not have happened.

236
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:06,170
Oh, that hurt a little.

237
00:15:06,170 --> 00:15:11,140
You dressing Eli up is merely an extension
of your own interests, right?

238
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:13,270
What a disrespectful son I have!

239
00:15:13,270 --> 00:15:16,480
If you are envious, you need simply
and honestly admit that you are.

240
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,320
Pardon me?

241
00:15:17,320 --> 00:15:21,480
Why must I be envious of my mother's silly hobby
of dressing up younger ladies?

242
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:25,450
And what, pray tell, are you trying to imply?

243
00:15:25,450 --> 00:15:26,740
Elianna.

244
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:31,990
If you're calling my wife "Mother,"
what will you call me?

245
00:15:33,250 --> 00:15:35,110
Well, since you’re the king, ‘Your Majesty’?

246
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:37,960
Eli.

247
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:41,630
You can call me your refined and kind uncle, if you'd like.

248
00:15:41,920 --> 00:15:45,010
What utter nonsense are you spewing?

249
00:15:45,010 --> 00:15:48,360
You're going to die a lonely death
as the bachelor you are, Uncle.

250
00:15:49,010 --> 00:15:52,350
It's taken four years of my life to get that name.

251
00:15:52,350 --> 00:15:56,060
How about you take the same time as I did and earn it?

252
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:59,150
It took quite a lot to get that name.

253
00:16:01,350 --> 00:16:02,400
Elianna.

254
00:16:02,830 --> 00:16:06,900
I heard that recently, you used your influences
in various ways for the Azul Region.

255
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:12,330
I commend you for those efforts, and I was thinking
I would give you some kind of reward.

256
00:16:12,330 --> 00:16:14,750
Oh, it was nothing at all.

257
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:17,000
Well, from the beginning of the year,

258
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:21,170
red dresses dyed with Milulu clams
will no doubt be in vogue.

259
00:16:21,710 --> 00:16:25,160
Your achievements will certainly become something huge.

260
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:26,920
No need to be so modest, just accept it.

261
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:32,500
But we don't know if this will make life
safe and secure in the Azul Region.

262
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:35,770
There was one other ink that you found, right, Eli?

263
00:16:35,770 --> 00:16:39,190
Eh? Yes, but that was...

264
00:16:39,190 --> 00:16:42,560
I've made use of it over there.

265
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:43,980
From next year on,

266
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:47,320
I want to make it one of the Holy Night's Banquet specialties.

267
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:51,030
That's why you should get your reward.

268
00:16:54,900 --> 00:17:01,960
Well then, may I take a short rest
when the Holy Night's Banquet is over?

269
00:17:02,380 --> 00:17:03,460
A break?

270
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:07,090
Yes. Well...

271
00:17:07,090 --> 00:17:09,470
I'd like to read some books.

272
00:17:09,470 --> 00:17:10,590
Books?

273
00:17:10,590 --> 00:17:11,640
Yes.

274
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:14,470
I've got a stack of many books I'd like to read.

275
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:20,230
There would be no greater reward
than being able to take a break, Your Majesty!

276
00:17:25,070 --> 00:17:26,000
Very well.

277
00:17:26,810 --> 00:17:28,860
Lady Elianna Bernstein.

278
00:17:29,470 --> 00:17:36,870
I grant you a vacation, and I vow to you
not a single soul shall stand in the way of that.

279
00:17:38,580 --> 00:17:41,370
Thank you, Your Majesty!

280
00:17:41,850 --> 00:17:44,380
You are way too soft with Elianna!

281
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:46,390
Not nearly as soft as you are...

282
00:18:36,300 --> 00:18:38,430
Eli... I'm sorry.

283
00:18:38,430 --> 00:18:39,310
Hm?

284
00:18:39,620 --> 00:18:44,310
I haven't kept the promise that I made to you
at the beginning at all.

285
00:18:44,990 --> 00:18:46,540
Lady Elianna,

286
00:18:46,540 --> 00:18:50,160
the only things you'll need to do
are stay by my side and read your books.

287
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:55,680
I decided for myself that I would be by your side.

288
00:18:56,480 --> 00:19:00,830
There are things I ought to do to that end,
so it's all right.

289
00:19:01,900 --> 00:19:06,790
I've only made you put up with everything,
and I am a disappointment of a prince.

290
00:19:07,690 --> 00:19:09,770
Your Highness, to me you're a dashing prince.

291
00:19:11,110 --> 00:19:14,840
You’re utterly amazing—more than I even deserve.

292
00:19:15,570 --> 00:19:22,470
In my eyes... you’re the best prince in the world.

293
00:19:25,970 --> 00:19:28,370
Say that once more, Eli.

294
00:19:29,790 --> 00:19:31,480
Once is enough.

295
00:19:36,010 --> 00:19:37,990
I wish I could get a reward, too.

296
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:42,470
I'd like to have some of your time.

297
00:19:43,530 --> 00:19:44,580
Is that too demanding?

298
00:19:44,580 --> 00:19:47,120
No, that's fine...

299
00:19:47,120 --> 00:19:48,250
Really?

300
00:19:50,210 --> 00:19:51,500
Of course.

301
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:54,510
That's a promise, Eli.

302
00:20:17,150 --> 00:20:20,450
Your Highness, is something happening here?

303
00:20:20,450 --> 00:20:23,860
Yeah. It's a special touch for tonight.

304
00:20:25,270 --> 00:20:26,560
Everyone,

305
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:32,420
I promise you all that this Holy Night's Banquet
will remain in your heart for eternity.

306
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:36,420
Keep your eyes peeled. You’re in for a real treat.

307
00:20:37,420 --> 00:20:38,430
Quench the braziers!

308
00:20:40,440 --> 00:20:42,180
Ready, and...

